{#
	What stands where a deferred widget is going to be (XIV-66).

	A placeholder rather than nothing, because the alternative is a page that
	visibly grows under the reader's cursor as each card lands — the layout shift
	that makes a fast page feel broken. This holds roughly the room a card takes
	and says, in text a screen reader will also read, that something is coming.

	Deliberately not a spinner. A spinner is an animation asserting that waiting is
	happening; on a dashboard where most cards arrive in a few hundred milliseconds
	it is a flash of movement that draws the eye to the one place nothing has
	happened yet.
#}
<div class="card" aria-busy="true">
	<div class="card-body text-body-secondary small">{{ 'dashboard.loading'|trans }}</div>
</div>
